-- title:
--   Taylor–Wiles construction: R_Q acting on the localised cohomology module
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain, complete for its maximal-ideal adic topology and with finite residue field $k$, and let $p$ be a prime with $p\neq 2$ and $p$ in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O$. Let $\bar\rho$ be a two-dimensional representation of $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ over $k$ trivial on some finite level, absolutely irreducible (irreducible after base change to $\overline k$). Let $S\supseteq S_{\min}$ be finite sets of primes with $p\in S_{\min}$, such that for primes $q\neq p$ one has $q\in S_{\min}$ exactly when $\bar\rho$ is ramified at $q$, and such that for $q\in S_{\min}$, $q\neq p$, every inertia element above $q$ has characteristic polynomial $(X-1)^2$ in $\bar\rho$. Let $N\neq 0$ be squarefree, prime to $p$, with all prime divisors in $S$, divisible by every $q\in S_{\min}\setminus\{p\}$, and with every prime divisor $\neq p$ lying in $S_{\min}$. Let $r\geq 5$ be a prime with $r\notin S$, $r\nmid Np$, $p\nmid r-1$, and $\operatorname{tr}\bar\rho(\sigma)^2\neq(r+1)^2$ for every Frobenius $\sigma$ at every valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ over $r$; assume weight-two cusp forms of level $N$ have an integral structure (the $\mathbb Z$-span of the forms with integral $q$-expansion coefficients spans over $\mathbb C$). Let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from the Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) (the $\mathbb Z$-algebra generated by the $T_\ell$, $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$, and the $U_q$, $q\mid N$) to $k$ satisfying $\det(X-\bar\rho(\mathrm{Frob}_\ell))=X^2-\theta(T_\ell)X+\ell$ for all primes $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$. Let $q_0,\dots,q_{t-1}$ be distinct primes, each $\geq 5$, none in $S$, each $\equiv 1 \pmod p$, and let $\alpha_i\in k$ be a simple root of $X^2-\theta(T_{q_i})X+q_i$ (so $2\alpha_i\neq\theta(T_{q_i})$). Let $D_{\min}$ be deformation-ring data for $\bar\rho$ of the minimal flat type [`GaloisRep.minimalFlatCondition 𝒪 p Smin`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L52) and $D_Q$ deformation-ring data for the type consisting of [`GaloisRep.flatCondition 𝒪 p (Smin ∪ {q_i})`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L47) together with unipotence on inertia at the primes $q\in S_{\min}$, $q\neq p$. Let $\varphi_0:D_{\min}.R\to\mathbb T:=$ [`CuspForm.heckeLocal N S 𝒪 θ`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) be a local $\mathcal O$-algebra map such that the base change of $D_{\min}.\rho$ along $\varphi_0$ has Frobenius characteristic polynomials $X^2-\pi(T_\ell)X+\ell$ for $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$. Let $\mathrm{cyc}_q$ be mod-$q$ cyclotomic characters, $\pi_{\Delta,q}:(\mathbb Z/q)^\times\to\mathbb Z/p^{v_p(q-1)}$ surjective for primes $q\neq p$, let $\varepsilon:D_Q.R\to D_{\min}.R$ be local with the base change of $D_Q.\rho$ along $\varepsilon$ equivalent to $D_{\min}.\rho$, and let $\iota:\mathcal O[\Delta]\to D_Q.R$, $\Delta=\prod_i\mathbb Z/p^{v_p(q_i-1)}$, satisfy $\varepsilon\circ\iota=1$ on group-like elements and diagonalise inertia at each $q_i$: there is a basis $b_0,b_1$ of $D_Q.\rho.V$ on which inertia above $q_i$ acts by $\iota$ of the $i$-th component character and its inverse. Assume the commutation hypotheses `OpComm` and `DiaComm` for the cohomology $H^1$ at level $N(\prod_i q_i)r$ with the subgroup $H_Q=H_R\cap\ker\pi_Q$, giving the localised module $M_Q:=$ `ML` of this Hecke data (localisation at the complement of the kernel of the character determined by $\theta$ on the $T_\ell$ and by $\alpha_i$ on $U_i$). Finally let $L$ be a $\mathbb T$-module, finite as $\mathcal O$-module, with compatible scalar towers, and $\lambda_L:M_Q\to L$ an $\mathcal O$-linear map carrying the action of each generator $T_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell\notin S$, $\ell$ not dividing the level) to multiplication by the image of $T_\ell$ in $\mathbb T$, and invariant under the diamond operators $\langle u\rangle$ on $M_Q$ for $u\in H_R$ (the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb Z/r)^\times$). Then there exist a group automorphism $\kappa$ of $\Delta$ and an $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism $\psi:D_Q.R\to\operatorname{End}_{\mathcal O}(M_Q)$ such that $\psi(\iota[\kappa(\pi_Q(u))])$ is the diamond operator attached to $u$ for every $u\in H_R$, and $\lambda_L(\psi(x)m)=\varphi_0(\varepsilon(x))\cdot\lambda_L(m)$ for all $x\in D_Q.R$ and $m\in M_Q$.
--
--   This is the Galois side of the Taylor–Wiles construction in the finite-flat case $p\nmid N$: the universal deformation ring of relaxed type at the auxiliary primes $Q=\{q_i\}$ acts on the localised degree-one cohomology module of the auxiliary level $\Gamma_0(N)\cap\Gamma_1(r)\cap\Gamma_{H_Q}(Q)$, so that the diamond operators coming from $\Delta_Q$ are realised through $\iota$ (up to the automorphism $\kappa$) and the action is compatible, via $\lambda_L$, with the minimal deformation ring mapping to the local Hecke ring. It is used by [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_taylorWilesModule_of_linearEquiv_ML_flat`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_taylorWilesModule_of_linearEquiv_ML_flat) to produce the Taylor–Wiles module over the group-ring $\mathcal O[\Delta_Q]$.
